		<PackageReleaseNotes>This release upgrades to NTokenizers 7.0.1 and reworks the Markdown renderer from a buffer-then-display model into a fully forward-only, per-token streaming pipeline, with a number of parsing and rendering fixes.

## Markdown streaming (rewrite)

- Markdown is now rendered forward-only: each token is written to the console as it arrives, the left side (borders, gutters, markers) is composed from the active nesting frame stack, and lines wrap only when a token no longer fits. The previous buffer-then-render LiveBlock model is gone.
- Nested Markdown (blockquote, heading, list items) is streamed token by token; list-item content can contain nested blocks such as quotes and lists.
- Root paragraphs are written directly and verbatim, so soft breaks inside a paragraph are preserved.
- Nested HTML style/script content is tokenized and streamed inline without the previous per-element handler delay.
- Nested list indentation and frame ordering are corrected.
- A pending block separator no longer renders as a blank line before a list's nested list.
- Console width is cached with a redirected-output fallback (80), removing the WindowWidth IOException when stdout is redirected.
- The unused generic Heading style property was removed; headings render through MarkdownHeadingStyles.

## Tables

- Tables render in a Spectre live region that grows and refreshes as rows arrive, restoring the previous growing-table behavior on the new streaming path.

## Writers

- The Emoji writer now supports the `:rocket:` short-code syntax.
- The Link writer rendering was improved.

## Dependencies

- Upgraded to NTokenizers 7.0.</PackageReleaseNotes>
